Document databases like MongoDB store data in flexible, semi-structured "documents" (often JSON or BSON). These documents can contain nested arrays and objects, providing a rich and hierarchical structure.
```json
{
  "_id": "user123",
  "name": "Alice Smith",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "addresses": [
    { "type": "home", "street": "123 Main St", "city": "Anytown" },
    { "type": "work", "street": "456 Oak Ave", "city": "Otherville" }
  ],
  "interests": ["coding", "hiking"]
}
```
